  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWhen looking into the [draggable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dnd.html#the-draggable-attribute) attribute I've noticed that it's \"enumerated\" rather than being a boolean attribute. At first this seems odd but actually makes sense, you can use draggable=\"false\" to disable the automatic behaviour of `<a href>` and `<img>`. A side effect of this is that `<div draggable>` *doesn't* make the element draggable.\n\nIs there a reason we don't special case the recently codified \"empty value default\" such that it matches the True state rather than the Auto state?\n\nIf there's not a compat concern it seems like it would make the attribute a bit more ergonomic and more consistent with attributes like popover?\n\nIf there is a compat issue it would be helpful to note this in the specification so that it's clear this unfortunate design is stuck this way.",
